WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.833
Hybrid search.

2
00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.834
Real queries mix concepts with part numbers.

3
00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.167
So run two retrievers, and merge them.

4
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.733
Here's the architecture.

5
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.300
The query goes to two retrievers at once.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.133
Dense search matches meaning, using vectors.

7
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:19.133
Sparse search, BM25, matches exact tokens.

8
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.967
Then Reciprocal Rank Fusion merges the two ranked lists.

9
00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.700
RRF is almost embarrassingly simple.

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.767
Each document gets one over k plus its rank, in each list.

11
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.633
K is about sixty, which softens the top.

12
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.223
Then we add up the scores across lists.

13
00:00:36.223 --> 00:00:39.100
Ranks are comparable even when raw scores aren't.

14
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.933
Let's try three documents.

15
00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:45.567
Document A is first by dense, but fifth by sparse.

16
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:49.367
Document B is second in both lists, and scores slightly higher.

17
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:53.509
Document C appears in only one list, so it scores lowest.

18
00:00:53.509 --> 00:00:55.667
Decent in both beats top in one.

19
00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:58.167
Here it is in Python.

20
00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.200
We loop over both ranked lists.

21
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.700
Each document accumulates one over k plus rank.

22
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.467
Then we sort by total score, highest first.

23
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:14.333
A flight controller asks about attitude drift involving IMU zero four B during the March burn.

24
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.333
Dense alone returns generic attitude chunks, the wrong unit.

25
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:24.267
BM25 alone returns every boring calibration sheet mentioning that part.

26
00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:28.433
The merge puts the one log about that unit and that burn at rank one.

27
00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:30.404
Let's recap.

28
00:01:30.404 --> 00:01:33.167
Run dense and sparse retrieval in parallel.

29
00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.733
Merge them with Reciprocal Rank Fusion.

30
00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.133
Ranks need no score normalization.

31
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:41.335
That makes it the enterprise default.

32
00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:42.433
Next up: BM25.
